    "created_at": "2024-07-23T02:43:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-07-23T02:43:01Z",
    "body": "> It may have been better to make the timeouts directly cancellable somehow, instantly releasing their timer IDs, as that is much closer to how real real browsers implement clearTimeout(), and the difference is technically observable if you somehow manage to exhaust all the timeout IDs. However, I couldn't work out how to do it that way in the specification language.\r\n\r\nHmm, why not use the \"next timer ID\" solution discussed in that issue?",
